**How to implement.** How a picked folder reaches the code and how an opened kit reaches its window leave the launcher for the kit-opening module, so the start screen calls the same code (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; step 154: a click starts the picker on the UI thread with `Async.StartImmediate`, `None` doing nothing; step 156: resolution on open). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs` (step 150), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2: (1) `type KitFolderPicker with member this.pickThen (onPicked : KitFolder -> unit) : unit` starts `this.pickKitFolder ()` with `Async.StartImmediate` and calls `onPicked` with the chosen folder; `None` (the user cancelled) calls nothing. It is step 154's body, moved, and adds no posting, retry or exception handling, because `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow` already answers `None` when the dialog cannot open (step 150). It is unique on its receiver beside `ofWindow` (ELEV019). (2) `OpenedKit` (step 150) gains `member this.resolveAndShow (imports : CatalogueImportContext) (show : OpenedKit -> unit) (onFailed : KitLibraryError -> unit) : unit`, step 156's resolution on open, moved. When `this.pendingDecisions` is empty it calls `show this`. Otherwise it shows `ImportDialogWindow(imports, ResolveKitSnapshot (this.library, this.decisions), onApplied)` (steps 108, 144) and no constructor yet; `onApplied applied` calls `this.withRebindings applied.outcome.rebindings` (step 150): `Ok resolved` calls `show resolved`, and `Error e` closes the kit (`this.library.kit.close ()`, step 131) and calls `onFailed e`. When the dialog closes without an Apply (its `Closed` with no `onApplied` before it, tracked by one local flag at this IO edge), the kit is closed and nothing else is called, so a cancelled resolution leaves the kit unlocked and the library unchanged. A close that fails is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying its `describe`, as `openKitAt` logs one. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow`: Main's and Inverse's clicks become `(pickerFor this).pickThen` of step 154's local function for the folder, the mode and `ReadWriteKitAccess`, and that function's `Ok opened` arm becomes `opened.resolveAndShow context.catalogueImports <show the constructor window of the mode> <show e.openFailedCaption in launcherKitErrorText>`, as step 154's open failures are shown. The launcher's own `Async.StartImmediate`, dialog, flag and re-binding code are deleted, and it behaves exactly as before. Tests: `KitOpeningTests` gains `pickThen hands on the folder the picker answers and nothing on a cancel`: a picker answering `Some` of a test-local folder at once calls `onPicked` once with it, and one answering `None` never calls it. `LauncherTests`' facts of steps 154 to 156 (`the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`, `a cancelled pick opens nothing`, the read-only offer and the three resolution facts) keep their assertions and pass over the moved code. The moved resolveAndShow behavior MUST retain step 156's all-Reuse confirmation test: pendingDecisions includes every snapshot row, and only an actually empty snapshot list bypasses the dialog.

**Acceptance.** After the pick and the hand-off move, `KitFolderPicker.pickThen` and `OpenedKit.resolveAndShow` MUST be the one home of the picker start and of resolution on open, and `LauncherWindow` MUST call them with no copy of its own; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `pickThen hands on the folder the picker answers and nothing on a cancel`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass, `LauncherTests`' facts of steps 154 to 156 included; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
